However, based on the comment "@@@ After the operation, the added element is stored at the first position," it seems there might be a misunderstanding. The method `addElement` adds the element to the end of the vector, not the first position. Therefore, the correct assert statement should check if the added element is at the last position:

<code>assert this.lastElement().equals(obj);</code>
